 host, multitude: -cārin, a. 🞄going about in troops (pl.);
 -nātha, m. lord 🞄or leader of a troop or herd: -pa, m. id. (said 🞄esp. of elephants);
 -pati, m. id.;
 -paribhraṣṭa, pp. strayed from the herd;
 -bhraṣṭa, 🞄pp. id.;
 -mukhya, m. chief of a host;
 -śas, 🞄ad. in flocks, herds, or troops;
 -agraṇī, m. 🞄leader of a host.
